# GitNexus ignore rules for HagenDa (Unity / Tuanjie project)
#
# Goal: the knowledge graph indexes SOURCE CODE ONLY. Prefabs, scenes,
# materials, imported model/texture/audio assets, Unity .meta sidecars and
# generated config are excluded so queries, execution flows and search results
# surface project code instead of asset noise.
#
# Why an extension deny-list instead of the usual "index only *.cs" whitelist
# idiom (`*` + `!*/` + `!*.cs`):
#   createIgnoreFilter() treats any `!pattern` in this file as an explicit
#   unignore that OVERRIDES the hardcoded DEFAULT_IGNORE_LIST *and* the earlier
#   .gitignore rules (last-match-wins, #771). A blanket `!*/` would therefore
#   re-enable traversal of Library/, Build/, Logs/, venv/ and node_modules/,
#   which .gitignore had excluded. Do NOT add directory negations here.
#
# Note: GitNexus only parses JS/TS/Python/Java/C/C++/ObjC/C#/Go/Ruby/Rust/PHP/
# Kotlin/Swift/Dart/Vue/Cobol/Zig. In this repo that means every symbol comes
# from .cs; the rules below exist to stop the non-code remainder from being
# read, stored and full-text indexed.

